libartnet
------------------------------------------
libartnet is an implementation of the ArtNet protocol for Linux, Mac, iOS, &
Windows (via mingw). ArtNet enables DMX512 and RDM data to be sent over IPv4
Networks. ArtNet was first developed in 2002 and is widely supported by
networked devices in the entertainment industry.

Runtime requirements:
  cygwin-3.6.12-1
  libartnet-devel-1.2.0-1bl2
  libartnet1-1.2.0-1bl2
  pkg-config-3.0.10-1

Build requirements:
(besides corresponding -devel packages)
  autoconf-20260320-3
  automake-20260320-2
  binutils-2.47-1
  cygport-0.37.12-1
  gcc-core-14.4.0-1
  libtool-2.6.2-1
  make-4.4.1-2

Canonical website:
  https://github.com/atlesn/libartnet

Canonical download:
  https://github.com/atlesn/libartnet/archive/refs/tags/v1.2.0.tar.gz

-------------------------------------------

Build instructions:
  1. unpack libartnet-1.2.0-X-src.tar.xz
  2. if you use setup to install this src package,
     it will be unpacked under /usr/src automatically
        % cd /usr/src
        % cygport ./libartnet-1.2.0-X.cygport all

This will create:
  /usr/src/libartnet-1.2.0-X-src.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libartnet-1.2.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libartnet1-1.2.0-X.tar.xz
  /usr/src/libartnet-devel-1.2.0-X.tar.xz

-------------------------------------------

